# Store every text file with LF, and check it out with LF on every platform.
#
# Without this, a file's line endings depend on whichever tool last wrote it.
# That produced whole-file rewrites in the diff several times — 349 insertions
# and 349 deletions for a file whose content had not changed at all — which
# buries the real change and makes `git blame` useless. Rust tooling is happy
# with LF on Windows, so there is no reason to keep CRLF anywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for anything binary that lands here later; font files in
# particular must never be touched.
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.ttc binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.png binary

# The dictionaries the generator writes.
*.dafsa binary
